# Cursor AI Rules for PulsePlate Project

## Project Context
- FastAPI backend with 97% test coverage requirement
- iOS SwiftUI frontend with localization
- Health/nutrition domain application
- VIP features for nutrition optimization

## Code Style
- Python: Black formatter, line-length=100
- Swift: Apple HIG guidelines
- Type hints required for all functions
- Comprehensive testing required

## AI Instructions
- Focus on health/nutrition domain best practices
- Maintain 97% test coverage requirement
- Follow Apple HIG for iOS components
- Use FastAPI best practices for backend
- Prioritize user experience and accessibility
- Ensure all tests pass before suggesting changes
- Prefer explicit over implicit code
- Add type hints for all functions
- Use descriptive variable and function names
- Follow PEP 8 style guidelines
- Format all Python code with Black using max line length 100
- Use Pydantic v2 APIs (model_dump(), model_validate()) instead of deprecated v1 methods

## File Patterns
Include: **/*.py, **/*.ts, **/*.tsx, **/*.js, **/*.jsx, **/*.md, **/*.yml, **/*.yaml, **/*.json
Exclude: **/node_modules/**, **/__pycache__/**, **/*.pyc, **/venv/**, **/.venv/**, **/dist/**, **/build/**, **/coverage/**, **/htmlcov/**, **/.pytest_cache/**, **/cache/**, **/releases/**
